gebaccauis.github.io/authors/hayato-ikoma/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Nov 2021 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://jorgebaccauis.github.io/authors/hayato-ikoma/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Samuel Pinilla</title><link>https://jorgebaccauis.github.io/authors/samuel-pinilla/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Nov 2021 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://jorgebaccauis.github.io/authors/samuel-pinilla/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Yifan Peng</title><link>https://jorgebaccauis.github.io/authors/yifan-peng/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Nov 2021 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://jorgebaccauis.github.io/authors/yifan-peng/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Karen Sanchez</title><link>https://jorgebaccauis.github.io/authors/karen-sanchez/</link><pubDate>Fri, 01 Oct 2021 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://jorgebaccauis.github.io/authors/karen-sanchez/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Sergio Castillo</title><link>https://jorgebaccauis.github.io/authors/sergio-castillo/</link><pubDate>Fri, 01 Oct 2021 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://jorgebaccauis.github.io/authors/sergio-castillo/</guid><description/></item><item><title/><link>https://jorgebaccauis.github.io/authors/admin/</link><pubDate>Tue, 05 Feb 2019 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://jorgebaccauis.github.io/authors/admin/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Jorge Bacca received the B.S. degree in Systems Engineering (&lt;em&gt;cum laude&lt;/em&gt;) and the Ph.D. degree in Computer Science (&lt;em&gt;laureate thesis&lt;/em&gt;) from the Universidad Industrial de Santander (UIS), Bucaramanga, Colombia, in 2017 and 2021, respectively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;He is an Assistant Professor in the Department of Systems and Informatics at UIS and the Founder and Director of the &lt;a href="https://pigroupuis.github.io/pigroup-research/"&gt;Inverse Problems Research Group (PI Group)&lt;/a&gt; (in formation). He is also a Postdoctoral and Visiting Researcher at GIPSA-lab, Université Grenoble Alpes (France) within the &lt;em&gt;PHAIMS&lt;/em&gt; project, and a Consulting Associate Editor for the &lt;em&gt;IEEE Open Journal of Signal Processing&lt;/em&gt;. He has authored 28 JCR journal papers (16 Q1) and more than 30 conference proceedings in computational imaging, inverse problems, and signal processing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;His current research interests include inverse problems, computational imaging, modulo imaging, unlimited sampling, optimization, spectral imaging, and deep learning.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>